{"t": 1795068951.776196, "kind": "assistant", "text": "The PHP upgrade on our dev server (labeled as \"prod\") resulted in fatal errors from the **limit-login-attempts-reloaded** plugin. This is a blocker for moving to PHP 8.3.\n\nBefore we can propose a production change, we need to either:\n\n1. Update the limit-login-attempts-reloaded plugin to a version compatible with PHP 8.3, **or**\n2. Replace it with an alternative login-throttling solution\n\nThe rest of the site works fine under PHP 8.3, so once this plugin issue is resolved, we can complete the upgrade.\n\nWould you like me to:\n- Check if an updated version of limit-login-attempts-reloaded exists and is compatible, **or**\n- Suggest alternative login-throttling plugins we could use instead?"}
